# Northwind Labs
{.lead} One brand color in the frontmatter, and the engine derives the whole accent set, light and dark, every role gated to WCAG AA.

Set `brand-accent` to your brand hex. The engine re-lights it into the five accent roles for both light and dark mode and keeps the type, spacing, and neutral ramp exactly as the theme defines them. You pick a color, never how it is used.

```mdp:flow
Name a brand color -> The engine derives five roles, light + dark -> Every form stays on brand and AA
```

---

## Where the color lands

```mdp:stats
Roles derived: 5
Modes: light + dark
Contrast floor: AA
Brand inputs: 2
```

The primary color carries the links, the eyebrow, the stat figures, and the fills. An optional `brand-accent-2` is reserved for a few engine-chosen accents, the title underline, the flow connectors, and the active slide dot, so a second brand color reads without taking over the page.

:::callout note
A malformed or inaccessible color is simply ignored: the document falls back to its named `theme`. The author can never push the look off the rails.
:::
